<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56790" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραύν-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Th.</u>
			430
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Ba.</u>
			594
		</span></i> (anap.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a
				thunderbolt</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βολαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλόξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1017
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέμφιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					538
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ, λαμπάδες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ba.</u>
				244
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span> death <i>by the
				thunderbolt</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				3.1.64
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>”
				<i>heliotrope,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					PHolm.
					10.37
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>VP</u>
				17
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				37.132
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>thundersmitten</i>, of Semele, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1139
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καπανέως κ. δέμας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					496
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Κεραύνια</span> the
				'<i>thunder-splitten peaks</i>', name of several mountain
			ridges, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.3.5
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραύνιος, ὁ</span>, kind of <i>bandage</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				<u>Fasc.</u>
				37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραύνειος, [Ζεύς</span>
			] <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				401a17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Milet.</u>
				1(7).278
			</span></i>; applied to Philip, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.115
			</span></i> (Antip. &lt;Sid.&gt;).</div>
